1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,790
Slide 6 brings an analogy every gamer will immediately understand: "THE 'OFFLINE LEVELING' ANALOGY!"

2
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:21,911
In early online RPG games, if you wanted your character to gain experience, you had to sit in a dark room for eight hours, clicking the exact same attack button against low-level monsters.

3
00:00:21,911 --> 00:00:23,670
That was manual grinding!

4
00:00:24,570 --> 00:00:26,779
Oh, man, I remember those days!

5
00:00:26,779 --> 00:00:28,561
My wrist hurt for a week!

6
00:00:28,561 --> 00:00:39,040
But look at how modern RPGs solved this: 'Offline Auto-Farming.' When you log off and go to bed, your character enters the automated training dojo.

7
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:47,979
And while you're asleep, the game engine calculates your training, gathers gold, cleans up your inventory, and levels up your skills!

8
00:00:48,879 --> 00:00:56,609
When you wake up, you don't grind goblins—you log in, gear up with the loot gathered overnight, and lead your guild into high-level boss raids!

9
00:00:57,509 --> 00:01:01,988
Gemini Spark is literally offline leveling for your professional life!

10
00:01:01,988 --> 00:01:11,139
While you sleep, it digests 40 research papers, filters your inbox, and tests your software code so you wake up ready for executive leadership!

11
00:01:12,039 --> 00:01:20,129
Gaming mastered this decades ago; today, we apply that exact architectural wisdom to enterprise intelligence.

